/*
# Disclosure

A section that opens and closes under a line that names it — "Advanced options", "Show
details". Press the line and the section slides open below it, its chevron turning as it
goes; press again and it slides shut. `Accordion` is a stack of these that keeps one open;
a `Disclosure` stands alone, and any number may be open.

The content is the disclosure's ordinary children, present through the whole slide and
carried by the disclosure's clip, exactly as an `Accordion`'s `AccordionPane` carries its own:

```declare
App [ width = 320, height = 200,
    Disclosure [ x = 20, y = 20, width = 280, label = "Advanced options",
        Checkbox [ label = "Keep a log" ],
        Checkbox [ label = "Check for updates" ]
        ]
    ]
```

To a screen reader the line is a button that says whether it is expanded; Tab reaches the
content only while it is open.

## label
The line's text, and the section's name.

## detail
A summary of what the section holds, set at the line's right end — "3 set", "12 files" —
so it reads whether the section is open or shut. Empty, the default, shows nothing.

## open
Whether the section is open. Constrain it to your own state and override `input` to own
the destination, or leave it alone and read it back.

## input()
**Where a toggle goes**, receiving the new `open`. The default writes `open`; override it to
own the destination.

## toggle()
Opens a closed section and closes an open one, routing through `input`. What the line's
press calls.

## _twist
**Internal.** The chevron's angle in radians, sprung between −π/2 (closed) and 0 (open) in step with the slide.

## clip
The section is carried by this clip while it slides: present the whole way, revealed and
concealed by the disclosure's own height.

## accessibilityRole
A group, named by its `label`; the line inside it is the button.

## accessibilityLabel
The `label`.

*/

include [ "control.declare", "icons/core.declare" ]

class Disclosure [ clip = true, width = 100%,
    label: string = "",
    detail: string = "",
    open: boolean = false,
    input(v: boolean) { open = v },
    toggle() { input(!open) },

    // where the content goes: the body, present only while open or sliding,
    // so Tab and a screen reader reach it only when it can be seen

    defaultPlacement = body,

    accessibilityRole = group,
    accessibilityLabel = { label },

    layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 0 ],

    // the slide: height springs between the bare line and the whole content,
    // and the clip carries the content the whole way

    slide: Spring [ attribute = height, to = { classroot.open ? classroot.contentHeight : classroot.line.height },
        stiffness = 220, damping = 26, epsilon = 0.4 ],
    _twist: number = { -Math.PI / 2 },
    Spring [ attribute = _twist, to = { classroot.open ? 0 : -Math.PI / 2 }, stiffness = 220, damping = 26, epsilon = 0.004 ],

    line: Control [ width = 100%, height = { provided("theme").accordionHeaderHeight },
        accessibilityRole = button,
        accessibilityExpanded = { classroot.open },
        press() { classroot.toggle() },
        cornerRadius = { provided("theme").controlCornerRadius },
        fill = { pressed ? provided("theme").controlPressed : hovered ? provided("theme").controlHovered : null },
        padding = [0, 10, 0, 8],
        layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = x, spacing = 8 ],
        chev: ChevronIcon [ y = center, iconSize = 14, angle = { classroot._twist }, ink = { provided("theme").textMuted } ],
        t: TextLabel [ shrinks = true, maxLines = 1, fontSize = { provided("theme").accordionFontSize }, fontWeight = medium,
            textColor = { provided("theme").text }, text = { classroot.label } ],
        Spacer [ ],
        more: TextLabel [ visible = { classroot.detail != "" }, wrap = false,
            fontSize = { provided("theme").accordionFontSize }, textColor = { provided("theme").textMuted }, text = { classroot.detail } ]
        ],

    body: View [ width = 100%, padding = [6, 0, 8, 30],
        layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 8 ],
        visible = { classroot.open || classroot.height > classroot.line.height + 0.5 }
        ]
    ]
